  "_comment": [
    "Editorial source for the curriculum. Hand-authored: this is where the",
    "teaching decisions live. `scripts/build_seed.mjs` expands it into the",
    "Firestore documents under seed/ — edit here, not there.",
    "",
    "Sequencing follows how pt-BR alphabetisation is normally taught:",
    "vowels first, then the consonants that form the simplest CV syllables",
    "(M, P), then voiced/voiceless pairs that teach a contrast (B/P, D/T,",
    "F/V, C/G, S/Z), then the digraphs (CH, LH, NH).",
    "",
    "Distractors are chosen to teach, not to pad: a lesson's tap options are",
    "letters the child has already met, and each `matchTrio` contrasts the",
    "new letter with its nearest confusable neighbour. Uppercase I is never",
    "placed beside L — they are the same glyph in most fonts.",
    "",
    "Listen words start with the letter being taught and are concrete enough",
    "for a 4-year-old to picture. Modules 6 and 7 switch to short phrases;",
    "see the README for what the activity engine still cannot express."
  ],
